+# One-index scoped context amendment
+
+`amend_scoped_context` runs only through the existing HTTP MCP server and its resident engine. It does not start a second PGLite process. It accepts only `{source_id, source_hash}` for an existing committed ingestion manifest. It reads that ingestion's private original to verify the supplied SHA-256 and extract the explicitly marked first-line title. A separate Jev request contains only that short title/evidence, never the original or private fact batch. Only a confident public verdict permits an index. Existing vault content, shared fact pages and placement manifests remain unchanged.
+
+The index at `mvp-shared:scoped-mvp/context/<sourceKey>` contains the approved title plus the current public bodies and plain-text references of exactly the manifest's already committed `mvp-shared` pages. No private page is copied into it. The `.scoped/context-amendments/<sourceKey>.json` audit records source hash, operator client, label, references, managed request ID and readback hash. A matching committed replay returns without classification or writes. A mismatch refuses. All classification and plan checks precede the publication marker. A failed write/readback leaves `publication-blocked` and the audit for operator recovery; it never retries as a generic write.
+
+## Operator-only invocation
+
+After deploying the operation code, use the already-running server's authenticated admin API to register a **new** confidential client. `POST /admin/api/register-client` requires its existing admin cookie/CSRF protections; a public request, ordinary bearer read token, or QM principal is not admin API authority. Request:
+
+```json
+{"name":"scoped-context-operator","scopes":["admin"],"source":"mvp-shared","federatedRead":["mvp-shared","mvp-vault"],"allowedOperations":["amend_scoped_context"],"surface":"full","grantTypes":["client_credentials"],"tokenEndpointAuthMethod":"client_secret_post"}
+```
+
+Store the returned credential privately; do not log the response or reuse the QM/capture credential. Mint its OAuth token through `/token` with `scope=admin`, then send a normal authenticated MCP `tools/call`:
+
+```json
+{"name":"amend_scoped_context","arguments":{"source_id":"<exact existing manifest sourceId>","source_hash":"<exact existing manifest sourceHash>"}}
+```
+
+The handler additionally requires HTTP, a verified OAuth-client principal, explicit admin scope, **exactly** this operation allow-list, shared write binding, and shared+vault read grants on the host brain. Any broader legacy token, QM bridge token, Telegram capture token, or caller role argument is rejected. Revoke the temporary client after successful verification. Do not delete a retained marker or alter a prior receipt to force retry. No live amendment has been performed by these tests or documentation.
