+# Scoped Brain MVP — historical foundation
+
+This document describes the original offline foundation and its regression fixture. For the current authenticated QM and Telegram workflow, use `SCOPED-QM-BRIDGE.md` and `integration/openclaw-telegram-capture/README.md`. This extension adds a trusted-local `scope` command to GBrain. It reuses the existing database and authenticated HTTP MCP server; it is not a separate service.
+
+## Fixed policy
+
+| Member | Readable sources |
+| --- | --- |
+| Iris | `mvp-shared` |
+| Elena | `mvp-shared`, `mvp-hr-payroll` |
+| Ben | `mvp-shared`, `mvp-juniper` |
+
+No member credential can read `mvp-vault`. Trusted local operators and anyone with filesystem/database ownership are outside this member boundary. Each new source explicitly disables automatic federation, so existing integrations do not silently gain access to it.
+
+Direct Anthropic Haiku extracts atomic facts with verbatim evidence. TypeSafe/Jev classifies them as shared, HR/Payroll, Juniper, both named scopes, or vault-only. Deterministic code places facts into GBrain sources, preserving the named-scope union rule. Every original remains in vault. Unsupported sensitive categories and low-confidence verdicts stay in vault; incomplete output or provider errors abort publication.
+
+## Operate
+
+Set an absolute `GBRAIN_HOME` for the existing brain. Take a consistent backup and stop its readers and writers before provisioning or ingestion. The tested deployment uses PGLite's exclusive datastore ownership; this is not an online multi-writer ingestion protocol.
+
+```sh
+bun run src/cli.ts scope provision
+bun run src/cli.ts scope ingest --id stable-document-identity --file /private/document.txt
+```
+
+Ingestion requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` in the operator's environment. Never put keys in arguments, documents, or source control. The bounded input limit is 20,000 characters and 30 extracted facts.
+
+Provisioning creates private member credential files under `$GBRAIN_HOME/.scoped/creds`. It refuses existing demo sources or credentials. Ingestion refuses a previously reserved document identity, even when its content changes. Do not change identities to bypass this restriction; updates and reclassification are outside the MVP.
+
+Publication uses GBrain's managed page-mutation API and checks each committed page by reading it back. A private ingestion manifest records progress. A `.scoped/publication-blocked` marker prevents the `serve` command from starting after an incomplete publication. Keep access closed and recover from a consistent backup or verify the incomplete publication as an operator; never clear this marker merely to make startup succeed.
+
+After successful ingestion, restart the existing server and integrations. Existing QM/OpenClaw connections remain bound to their original source. They are not a per-member scoped interface.
+
+## Reproduce the bounded demonstration
+
+The independent fixture is `test/scoped-mvp-fixture.json`. Only its document contents are ingestion inputs; its expectations are not model inputs.
+
+```sh
+bun scripts/scoped-mvp-eval.ts --export-documents /private/documents.json
+bun scripts/scoped-mvp-eval.ts \
+  --credentials "$GBRAIN_HOME/.scoped/creds" \
+  --manifest /private/verified-probe-manifest.json \
+  --out /private/new-report.json
+```
+
+The probe manifest contains actual `{sourceId,slug}` page references and `vaultExistenceVerifiedByOwner:true`, set only after an operator verifies vault readback. Restricted positive-control pages must contain the fixture's known values. Additional extracted helper pages can be tested separately, but the positive-control scorer deliberately fails when a requested page lacks a known test value.
+
+The evaluator obtains distinct OAuth tokens and checks complete raw MCP outputs. It requires all expected allowed values, rejects forbidden values, and treats transport errors or empty successes as failures rather than successful denials. Preserve unsuccessful reports as well as the final result.
+
+This is a small synthetic demonstration, not a general privacy proof. It does not implement dynamic membership, reclassification, Personal/manager-copy policy, embeddings, dream-cycle enforcement, a UI, scoped QM identity routing, or an exhaustive tool-surface audit.
