+# Scoped MVP QM bridge (integration contract)
+
+This patch defines the `qm_recall` MCP operation; it does not provision a live client or change QM. A trusted operator may call `provisionQmBridge(engine)` **only after** the four MVP sources and existing `default` source exist. It creates a confidential OAuth client named `mvp-qm-bridge` with `read` scope, federated grant for `mvp-shared`, `mvp-hr-payroll`, `mvp-juniper`, `mvp-vault`, `default`, `surface=full`, and the **atomic** operation allow-list `['qm_recall']`. Store its returned secret privately; never use an old member credential or expose any generic search/get-page tool with this credential. A second provisioning attempt refuses the existing client.
+
+The trusted operator must set GBrain config key `scoped.qm_bridge` to JSON with the exact registered client ID and QM-authenticated principal strings, after verifying both personal conversation scope formatting and the server-side QM identity binding:
+
+```json
+{"clientId":"<actual registered bridge client ID>","verifiedPersonalScopeFormat":"personal:<principal>","principals":{"admin":"<exact verified QM admin principal>","intern":"<exact verified QM intern principal>"}}
+```
+
+This format marker is an operator attestation, not evidence from the user message. QM verified the wire shape `personal:<actor.id>`; the lead must still confirm the actual principal IDs from authenticated sessions before setting the mapping. The intended portal mapping is the verified existing admin principal (for example, `admin-principal`) and the new intern principal (for example, `intern-principal`), not display names or user-supplied labels. QM's trusted provider must forward `query`, `acting_user`, `qm_scope`, and `conversation_scope` without sourcing identity from prompt/tool arguments the user can edit. GBrain cannot authenticate a forwarded per-user claim through a shared client credential; that binding must be enforced by QM. No `client_id`, `role`, or requested `source_id` input is accepted by this operation.
+
+Only an admin principal in the configured roster with both scopes exactly equal to `personal:<that principal>` reads all four MVP sources plus existing `default` memory, including vault. The configured intern, unknown users, missing fields, mismatched scopes, and rooms read `mvp-shared` only. The operation computes a **subset of the verified OAuth grant** before calling GBrain's existing `recall` implementation; incomplete source grants fall back to shared only. For an authorized admin personal call only, it also searches the vault source for `scoped-mvp/` pages and the existing `default` source for matching private pages/facts. This narrow supplement is necessary because normal remote recall deliberately hides `visibility: private` pages and facts; it never changes those global filters. `qm_recall` emits one whitespace-normalized, bounded text line (ranked page snippets, private source-bound bodies/facts, then ordinary fact text with real fact IDs), because QM query keeps only the first 20 physical MCP text lines and GBrain pretty-prints object responses. Existing Iris/Elena/Ben clients are unchanged. QM verified that a DM's conversation scope is `personal:<actor.id>`; configure the exact server-side admin/intern actor IDs, not display names, before enabling admin access.
+
+The shared MCP dispatcher checks `$GBRAIN_HOME/.scoped/publication-blocked` before and after remote read handlers and once more immediately before returning the response. When the existing publisher has marked a partial publication, it returns `unavailable` with no content; remote write/ingestion operations are not blocked by this read gate. An inaccessible marker path fails closed, and `qm_recall` also refuses an absent `GBRAIN_HOME`. This applies to generic read tools as well as `qm_recall`, so old connectors cannot read a partially published scoped document.
